Package: plateforce
Title: Force-Plate Jump Kinetics that Carry Their Method
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    c(
      person("Alex", "Harrison", email = "alex@saturdaymorning.fit",
             role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
      person("The authors of the bundled Rust crates", role = "ctb",
             comment = "See inst/AUTHORS for details")
    )
Description: Computes jump kinetics from a vertical ground reaction force
    trace. Every value carries the method that produced it: the rule, its
    published parameters, its citation and the choices made upstream of it.
    Across 244 trials from Harrison (2011) <doi:10.25710/929y-2n46>, ten
    published ways of computing one jump height disagree by a median 3.51
    cm, exceeding the study's 1.98 cm training effect, so the method is
    reported with the number. Authorship and licences of the bundled Rust
    sources are listed in the AUTHORS file of the installed package.
